---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="tharavad">
  <h1>tharavad</h1>

  <p>
    <strong>tharavad</strong> (tharavadu) is malayalam for the ancestral home.
    the big old house where the whole extended family lives. that's the model.
    not a product with a login page. a house with keys.
  </p>

  <h2>what</h2>

  <p>
    one server in a hackerspace in kerala. you open a pull request, someone
    reads it, you get a linux machine with your name on it.
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li><code>ssh you@you.tharavad.xyz</code> from anywhere</li>
    <li>root on your own nixos vm. your mess stays yours</li>
    <li>a port in git → <code>https://you.tharavad.xyz</code></li>
  </ul>

  <p>no signup form. no credit card. no ticket. <a href="/join/">join</a>.</p>

  <h2>why</h2>

  <p>
    most people who wanted a box at 13 never got one. signup walls, cards,
    "contact sales". the useful rooms closed when the forums did. we can't fix
    that. we can keep one house open.
  </p>

  <p>
    renting teaches you someone's billing page. owning teaches you watts,
    disks, packets, boot order. that stuff is true everywhere. and when you
    can't buy more compute, you write better code.
  </p>

  <p>
    git is the guest list. your access is a file in a public repo. who's in,
    who let them in, when, why: <code>git log</code>. no secret admin list. no
    favours.
  </p>

  <p>
    break it. nothing in here is precious. the whole house builds from one repo,
    so when it falls over we put it back and time how long that took. then we
    make the number smaller.
  </p>

  <h2>how</h2>

  <p>
    a used dell r730xd. 88 threads, 62 GB, 151 W idle. one small vps in front
    as the door. the space's firewall. all of it is one
    <a href="https://nixos.org">nix</a> flake:
    <a href="https://github.com/tinkerhub0/mothership">tinkerhub0/mothership</a>.
    the <a href="https://github.com/tinkerhub0/mothership/tree/main/docs">docs</a>
    are written for people who've never done this before.
  </p>

  <p>
    <a href="https://tinkerhub.org">tinkerhub</a> bought the iron. we run it.
  </p>

  <p>
    <a href="/join/">join</a> · <a href="/house/">who's here</a> ·
    <a href="/log/">ship log</a> · <a href="/about/">longer story</a> ·
    <a href="/blog/">notes</a>
  </p>
</Base>
